From dbaeef363ea54f4c18112874b77503c72ba60fec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Emilsson <jonas.emilsson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: Guard intel_mst_reprobe_topology against torn-down MST manager

A hotplug or link-loss event can tear down the MST topology
(setting mgr->mst_state = false and mgr->mst_primary = NULL) concurrently
with a modeset that calls intel_mst_reprobe_topology(). This causes
drm_dp_mst_topology_queue_probe() to fire its WARN_ON:

  WARN_ON(!mgr->mst_state || !mgr->mst_primary)

at drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_topology.c:3741, which was observed
crashing the Hyprland compositor on a ThinkPad X1 Carbon (11th gen) with
Intel Raptor Lake Iris Xe graphics when connecting/disconnecting DP MST
monitors.

Fix this by checking mst_state and mst_primary under mgr->lock before
calling queue_probe, mirroring the analogous fix made for the AMD driver
in commit 62320fb8d91a ("drm/amd/display: Enable mst when it's detected
but yet to be initialized").

mgr->lock protects both mst_state and mst_primary as documented in
include/drm/display/drm_dp_mst_helper.h. The lock is released before
calling drm_dp_mst_topology_queue_probe(), which re-acquires it
internally, to avoid deadlock.

intel_mst_set_probed_link_params() is called unconditionally so that
cached link parameters remain current for the next MST session.

Fixes: dbaeef363ea5 ("drm/dp_mst: Add a helper to queue a topology probe")
Cc: Imre Deak <imre.deak@intel.com>
Cc: Lyude Paul <lyude@redhat.com>
Cc: intel-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org
Cc: dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org
Signed-off-by: Jonas Emilsson <jonas.emilsson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_mst.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_mst.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_mst.c
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_mst.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_mst.c
@@ -1188,10 +1188,17 @@ static void intel_mst_reprobe_topology(struct intel_dp *intel_dp,
 				       const struct intel_crtc_state *crtc_state)
 {
+	bool can_probe;
+
 	if (intel_mst_probed_link_params_valid(intel_dp,
 					       crtc_state->port_clock, crtc_state->lane_count))
 		return;

-	drm_dp_mst_topology_queue_probe(&intel_dp->mst.mgr);
+	mutex_lock(&intel_dp->mst.mgr.lock);
+	can_probe = intel_dp->mst.mgr.mst_state && intel_dp->mst.mgr.mst_primary;
+	mutex_unlock(&intel_dp->mst.mgr.lock);
+
+	if (can_probe)
+		drm_dp_mst_topology_queue_probe(&intel_dp->mst.mgr);

 	intel_mst_set_probed_link_params(intel_dp,
 					 crtc_state->port_clock, crtc_state->lane_count);
--
